{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":296638,"name":"Jeremy Hylton","username":"jhylton","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/jhylton/{size}/5594_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-15T23:17:04.653Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eGuido and I were looking at an old bug this week. It’s about an inconsistency in how variables are resolved in class namespaces. There are several possible solutions, including closing the bug as “working as intended.” I drafted a PEP to describe the problem and propose three non-trivial solutions. I’d be interested to hear which of the approaches in the PEP seem reasonable to people.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0840/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/7/8/7808f673c94c5abc6cdd738548e39c7ae50dc418.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"979F6B\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0840/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ePython Enhancement Proposals (PEPs)\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cimg width=\"200\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/8/e/8eb386d43fc93f43e4e34ee56dd1c3ebf682e66d.png\" class=\"thumbnail onebox-avatar\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"9EAC81\"\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0840/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ePEP 840 – Name Resolution in Class Namespaces | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eThere is a long-standing inconsistency in the way variable names are resolved in classes.  Several alternatives to resolve this inconsistency are discussed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: 